            <title><![CDATA[Western states face more water cutbacks as Colorado River shrinks]]></title>
            <link>https://www.pbs.org/newshour/show/western-states-face-more-water-cutbacks-as-colorado-river-shrinks</link>
            <description><![CDATA[After years of battles over its use — and a long-running drought — states that rely on the Colorado River are facing the prospect of further cutbacks. Years of gridlock among the states prompted the federal government to step in.  A new blueprint lays out new requirements for managing the shrinking river. Science correspondent Miles O'Brien explains what's at stake for our series, Tipping Point.]]></description>
